      <title>Meta Earnings: Investors Look to Zuckerberg for the Muse Payoff</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-21/meta-earnings-investors-look-to-zuckerberg-for-the-muse-payoff</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">039b092f8b1e010adea738f6</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:30:09 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Meta Platforms Inc. leads the tech pack this week, reporting its third-quarter earnings a week ahead of most of its peers. Take that as a sign of confidence, perhaps. The positive reception to the company’s Muse assistant has Wall Street investors wondering whether the personal artificial-intelligence agent is proof of an AI business model they have been desperately seeking.</description>
