      <title>Flu Has Landed Early — And You’re Past Due on Getting Vaccinated</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-21/flu-has-landed-early-and-you-re-past-due-on-getting-vaccinated</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">8444e8920708f535f246a2d1</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:30:08 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>This fall, like every other, I tried to game the flu season. My goal, always, is to get my vaccine at just the right moment: before the first cases pop up, yet late enough so that its protective effects last beyond the holidays and well into January or February, when infections tend to peak. That typically means scheduling my appointment for sometime in mid-to-late October.</description>
      <dc:creator>Lisa Jarvis</dc:creator>
